     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><br>Hi everyone,<div><br></div><div>After installing the new version of geomorph (3.3.1), I&#39;ve run into an error when trying to perform PCA.</div><div><br></div><div><pre style=\"font-family:Monaco,monospace,monospace;font-size:12px;outline:none;border-width:initial;border-style:none;word-break:break-all;line-height:1.45;color:rgb(0,0,0);white-space:pre-wrap!important\"><span style=\"color:blue;white-space:pre\">&gt; </span><span style=\"color:blue\">data(plethspecies) \n</span><span style=\"color:blue;white-space:pre\">&gt; </span><span style=\"color:blue\">Y.gpa &lt;- gpagen(plethspecies$land)   \n</span><span style=\"outline:none;border-width:initial;border-style:none;word-break:break-all\">  |============================================================================================================| 100%\n</span><span style=\"color:blue;white-space:pre\">&gt; </span><span style=\"color:blue\">PCA &lt;- gm.prcomp(Y.gpa$coords)\n</span><span style=\"color:rgb(197,6,11)\">Error in do.call(ordinate, ord.args) : object &#39;ordinate&#39; not found</span></pre></div><div><br></div><div>I have another system where 3.3.0 is still installed, and it works just fine there. Any suggestions?</div><div><br></div><div>Best,</div><div>Dave Angelini</div></div>"
    ]
   ]
  },
